A||N||6||FieroJoe||Under-seat aftermarket switch mounting||||6||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||03-10-2001||10:00 PM||||Thought I would share my idea that I had been toying around for a while come reality.<P>With all the new electronic goodies that I am putting in, I need a few switches and pushbuttons.  I dont like the idea of mounting them anywhere I can find by means of cutting trim panels, so I thought I could mount them under the seat where I could reach them when the need came.<P>Here are some pics:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/panelinstall3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/panel1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/panelstanchions.jpg"> <P>TFTS||||reg||6
Z||000001||rodmcneill||03-10-2001||10:15 PM||||Which button is the ejector seat?||||reg||12
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||03-10-2001||10:24 PM||||Don't hit the eject thinking it's the NOS<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||03-10-2001||10:54 PM||||haha, no ejector seat yet.  maybe if I had a targa top...||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||03-11-2001||10:55 AM||||Nice idea.  I have a thought, though.  Won't it be hard to push the button or flip the switch when you're sitting down?  The seats are so low to the ground.  Good idea!||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||03-11-2001||01:43 PM||||That't not a bad idea.... <P>1 sugestion. tie the harness off to one of the 2 hog rings to prevent it flexing or pulling as the seat is moved. The one closer to the seat lever looks like it would keep the cable from rubbing it as well. I know most people don't move the seat much, just gives a little extra protection.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||03-11-2001||09:00 PM||||yeah, I do have to lean a little bit forward to get at the switches, but I knew that while I was making it, and the switches arent always going to be used everytime I drive my car.<P>I did realize that there was going to need to be some movement under the seat, that's why the wiring harness I made is long, and there will also be enough of the other end of it that comes out of the carpet to allow for movement.  That is also why I used the insulated type connectors, so incase they do touch, they wont short out.  I was also planning on using tie wraps to secure them to sometime, I'll try to hog rings.<P>Thanks for the comments.||||reg||1
